@1101 = ~Incarnation of the spirit of the great worm~
@1102 = ~Get rid of this parasite for me.~
@1103 = ~Adventurers? Here? Finally! If you found your way in, you know your way out. Tell me!~
@1104 = ~I must destroy the boss of this area to obtain a rune, and then use that rune.~
@1105 = ~If you are the boss, you should know.~
@1106 = ~A spirit asked me to get rid of you. Prepare to die.~
@1107 = ~I don't have a rune. I don't know what rune you're talking about.... You're lying! Never mind, I'll find a way over your dead body.~
@1108 = ~You're telling me that I should know? I've been holed up in this tiny place for over 20 years, doing nothing but fending off attempts by those filthy lizards to get in, with no glimpse of a way out, and you're telling me that I should know? Unless... You're accusing me of lying, are you? The thief accused me of lying too... he got what he deserved. And it will be the same for you.~
@1109 = ~A spirit? There's no spirit up there, just those damn lizards. I know! You're trying to confuse me. The paladin tried to confuse me too. He died for it. And you'll die too.~
@11010 = ~Letter~
@11011 = ~JI'm going mad. They're all dead. Dead. I'm the only one still alive. I was the smartest. Now I'm nothing, and I'm going mad. I can hear them stomping around upstairs. They want to get in. But they won't get in. Every day, I've placed an anti-dragonnid glyph. There are so many that even those damn ghosts won't be able to remove them. I won't die. I've survived this far, and I'll survive again. Without my wand, I would have been dead long ago, but my wand keeps me alive. Well, live... is it a life to no longer eat or drink? Raah! I'm going crazy. And this place, ridiculously small, does it exist or did I imagine it? My prayers remain unanswered. The spells come to me like every morning, but I haven't heard the voice of my god since that Cursed day when we entered this hellish journey. There were eight of us. Or seven, I can't remember. We were powerful, and sure of ourselves... nonsense. No one is ever powerful enough. The elf fell first when the chasm swallowed her. The paladin's grief was fatal. The sorceress was prepared for anything, but not for the thief's treachery. The barbarian shouldn't have gotten involved... the thief had planned everything. Except losing his head to the dwarf's axe. There were only three of us left when we saw the dragons. They ate the dwarf and the warrior. I rushed into that hole and cursed them all for leaving me alone. Shalierra...  Why did you leave me? Why did you let Blackhand attack you? Didn't you see it coming? Really? Or did you do it on purpose? This journey is driving us all mad, but I was already mad from the moment I met you. Oh... Shalierra... can you see me from where you are?
Ha, they're scratching again. Let them come. I've set traps. Dragons though they may be, they won't be able to resist a finger of death enhanced by years of preparation. Let them come, and maybe this nightmare will end. Shalierra, I'm coming...~